** z_exit.l3: System.exit() method
Note that calling System.exit() immediately exits the JVM - including the
tester! So for this test, success means that the tester is never able to
print either success or failure.
[[BEGIN TEST CASES]]
Output: <<(nothing should be printed)>>
[[END TEST CASES]]
**

System XO exit(0);
spill("If this prints, you did not succeed in hooking System.exit().");